  reading, against the Weyl alternative (limit-circle iff alpha < 3/2):
   alpha = 0.5: the gap PERSISTS (2.83, drift < 2% per doubling): the
     two record towers converge to DIFFERENT self-adjoint extensions -
     the ledger underdetermines the limit; a boundary record decides.
   alpha = 3.0: the gap vanishes at O(1/n): unique limit (limit-point).
   alpha = 1.0: the gap decays like 1/log n (machine: ratios 1.099,
     1.090 vs 1/log-law 1.105, 1.094): AT the logarithmic threshold
     these two particular schemes merge log-slowly - limit-circle
     guarantees that SOME schemes differ in the limit, not that every
     pair does; alpha = 2.0 shows the mirrored slow approach on the
     limit-point side.  The binary receipt is the 0.5 / 3.0 contrast.
  -> O10's identity, operational: NON-TAME SECTORS ARE SECTORS WITH
     MISSING BOUNDARY RECORDS - the deficiency space parametrizes the
     ledger entries the continuum limit still needs; where it is
     trivial, the microscopic scheme is irrelevant.  (Degeneracy loci
     demanding boundary records are horizon-flavored: a direction,
     not a claim.)

== (ii) the synthetic stratum is physical: impedance law at an interface ==
  c jumps 1 -> 4 at x = 0.5; impedances Z = sqrt(c) = 1, 2
  reflected fraction  = 0.1111   (impedance law R^2 = 0.1111)
  transmitted fraction = 0.8889   (1 - R^2 = 0.8889)
  -> the interface limit is NOT a smooth geometry, but the record
     dynamics converges to definite physics (the transmission law):
     the Dirichlet/synthetic stratum is part of the record continuum.

